.TH WSLX 1 "September 2026" "WSLX 0.1.0-dev" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wslx \- Windows and WSL productivity toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wslx
.RI < path >
.br
.B wslx path
.RI [ options ] " <path>"
.br
.B wslx
.RI --win " <path>"
.br
.B wslx
.RI --link " <path>"
.br
.B wslx
.RI < command > " [options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
WSLX is a small command-line toolkit for Windows and WSL interoperability.
The path command normalizes Windows paths for use in WSL by default, while
explicit options can return Windows form or an interactive hyperlink.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B path
Make a path usable in WSL. Windows drive paths are converted; WSL/Linux paths
remain unchanged.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the current WSLX environment and installation.
.TP
.B version
Print the installed version.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove the current-user installation.
.TP
.B help
Show top-level help.
.SH PATH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --wsl
Return WSL form. This is the default path behavior.
.TP
.B --win
Return the Windows representation of a path.
.TP
.B --link
Display the Windows representation as an OSC-8 terminal hyperlink when stdout
is interactive. Non-interactive output is plain text.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show path-specific help when used with the path command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B wslx 'D:\Programming\Test'
Print /mnt/d/Programming/Test.
.TP
.B wslx /mnt/d/Programming/Test
Keep the WSL path unchanged.
.TP
.B wslx --win /mnt/d/Programming/Test
Print D:\Programming\Test.
.TP
.B wslx --link /mnt/d/Programming/Test
Show the Windows path as a clickable link when the terminal supports it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/wslx
Default CLI entry point.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/wslx
Default WSLX data directory.
.TP
.I ~/.bashrc
Contains one optional, clearly marked WSLX managed block.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR wslpath (1)
